candidate_text:
Position: CFO
Moreinfo: International accountant in group companies Capitalix
Functional responsibilities:
- Accounting for Capitalix Group companies registered in
United Kingdom and Estonia, Hong Kong, United Arab Emirates, Cyprus, Sweden, using the SAP accounting software;
- formation and execution of payments on the company's accounts;
- cash accounting, banking operations (work in client-bank), experience
of working with foreign banks;
- work with primary and consolidated documentation (invoices, acts of work performed, acts of
reconciliations), preparation of documents, including invoices for payment in accordance with the concluded contracts of the Group companies;
- collection, systematisation and preparation of data for reporting on the activities of the Group companies;
- drafting contracts, monitoring compliance with their execution;
- conducting business correspondence with foreign counterparties, maintaining communications with foreign partners of the Group's companies;
- Preparing management reports for the company's management.
Chief Accountant: August 2019 - to date, the group of companies 4bill 
Functional responsibilities: 
-	participation in the verification and approval of contracts with contractors and related documents;
-	preparation and submission of financial, accounting, tax and statistical reports, reporting to the NBU
-	passing the annual external audit
-	implementation, optimization of the program 1C 8.3 for the specifics of the enterprise. Statement and development of tasks for the programmer.
-	optimization of taxation within the legislation;
-	management of accounting services of enterprises belonging to the company group;
-	control and analysis of the use of the company's budget;
-	introduction of accounting for new activities and control over them
-	development of an automated system for reconciliations and reporting to management;
-	management and control of personnel of 3 people
Chief Accountant : December 2017 - August 2019 PAE "Pereselenske-K", Kyiv Functional responsibilities: 
-	accounting for settlements with debtors and creditors;
-	control of receivables and payables (organization of reconciliation with counterparties);
-	control over the accounting of finished products;
-	organization and control over the inventory;
-	registration of tax invoices, adjustments to tax invoices;
-	control over the limit for registration of tax invoices, tax credit, tax liability;
English Level: intermediate
Experience Years: 6.0
