Position: Business Analyst
Moreinfo: Hi! Nice to see you here!

Please check quick introduction about me:

- Almost 5 years of experience in software development as a Business Analyst and a Product Owner;
- Defining and managing Product Goal, Vision, Roadmap, and Product Backlog; 
- Creating Customer Journey Map, Story Mapping, UX mocks, MVP scope, etc.;
- Conducting NPS survey, interview, brainstorming, and workshop sessions; 
- Defining the customers' needs and translating them as User Stories and Use Case Scenarios;
- Facilitating Sprint Planning, Refinement, and Sprint Review events; 
- Providing design review and increment acceptance, planning Product Releases;
- Collaboration with team members, Product Managers, customers, end-users, and stakeholders.

My top 3 oriented values:
- Customer-centricity in the developing products;
- Transparency in the process and communication;
- Respect and trust as core values for successful relationships. 

I'm happy to talk to you, message me :)
Highlights: - Led discovery phase for and succeeded in solving the scope
- Used UX prototyping tools to validate requirements and provide UX recommendations
- Built the well-organized confluence space with all project requirements
- Organized workshop with focus group of end users to elicit requirements and align their expectations
- Carried out the research of the products to provide better business value for the customer

Experience in domains: 
Healthcare, Artificial Intelligence, Augmented reality, Smart home, Sports betting platform, Blockchain, Big data and e-commerce.

Certifications: 
- Professional Scrum Product Owner™ I (PSPO I)
- Professional Scrum Master™ I (PSM I)
- Blockchain Basics
- Introduction to Big Data
- Machine learning in Production
