candidate_text:
Position: Back-end | Full Stack (Node.js/React/TypeScript)
Moreinfo: Over 3 years of experience:
- two years as a Front-end developer;
- for the last year - I've been working as a Back-end developer.

Primary stack:
- TypeScript;
- JavaScript (ES6);
- Node.js (Express, Nest.js);
- AWS (Serverless Framework);
- React;
- Redux (Thunk, Saga);
- PostgresSQL | MongoDB | DynamoDB;
- Webpack;
- Docker;
- Unit tests (TDD);

As a Front-end developer, I had challenging tasks such as creating a Chrome extension, Electron App, Server-Side Rendering.
As a Back-end developer, I usually do Serverless app. It also may be dockerized node.js app, microservices or monolith.

Currently I'm working on the project with the following stack: Node.JS + TypeScript + AWS + Serverless + PostgresSQL + DynamoDB.
Looking For: Desired position: Back-end / Full Stack with primary Back-end responsibilities. TypeScript is essential. Prefer big companies. Remote-first, flexible schedule, office in Kyiv would be a plus.

P.S. I do not want to take a Front-end position - want to move forward as a solid Back-end developer.
