candidate_text:
Position: Business Analyst
Moreinfo: Greetings! 

For nine years, I've been developing and supporting projects related to different domains such as financial, law enforcement, banking, administration of the city, energy industry
Some projects combine the role of proxy product owner and business analyst.

My key responsibilities:
• gathering, analyzing, and documenting customer requirements;
• writing detailed product specifications (Functional requirements, Non-Functional requirements, User Stories)
• Collaboration with UX/UI designer in creating interactive prototypes for stakeholders and the development team;
• prioritizing tasks, backlog management;
• using agile and waterfall methodologies;
• Led sprint planning meetings, PBR, Daily scrum meetings, Demo;
• planning, organizing, and conducting business process reengineering

Agile, business analysis, problem-solving, Scrum, user stories, BPMN, Waterfall, Managing requirements, Draw.io, SDLC, MS Visio, Figma, User Story Mapping

I am interested in innovative projects and new technologies.
Looking For: 1. I do not want to test features myself, as the Quality Assurance role exists for this purpose. I can only contribute to QA in order to test the features and monitor if anything works as promised.

2. I don't want to design the interface of the software myself, as for this role UX/UI role exist. I can contribute in monitoring the logic of flow which designer make while designing software interface or collaborate with this role holder in order to create interactive prototypes.
English Level: upper
Experience Years: 9.0
